  "behavior": [
    "Confirmed task death invalidates checkImage even when the pinned old mm is live; imageRetired remains false to preserve native-call cleanup through surviving siblings.",
    "Owner-only retry restores pending marker and owned private code bytes via the pinned old descriptor, preserving unowned byte bits and independently checking kernel-applied writes.",
    "Failed marker/code restoration remains retryable without reopening a dead/reused TID, mutating saved registers/masks, or tracing the CLONE_VM peer.",
    "Terminal event ownership alternates between actual recovery wait and caller reaping; each row verifies original 32-byte scratch and actual peer death/mm retirement."
  ],
  "proofLimits": [
    "ELF64 target interrupted in actual i386 INT80 nanosleep restart-block; private caller-owned scratch and writable pinned old memory required.",
    "Fourteen ABI/mask failures plus three held SIGSTOP/LISTEN states and two probe failure rows; other task-death/reuse race windows remain open.",
    "No independent allocator owner unmaps a retained old frame through a separate CLONE_VM peer; tests reclaim remaining allocations through actual peer exit.",
    "Alive completed-ticket affinity, borrowed/quiesced and read-only transports, synchronous delivery, syscall policies, cancellation/shutdown, nonleader exec and other restart classes remain unfinished.",
